2 = 10201 × 10201. 10201 × 10000 = 102010000. 10201 × 201 = 10201 × 200 + 10201 = 2040200 + 10201 = 2050401. Total = 102010000 + 2050401 = 104060401. \n\nSo 104060401 = 10201^2!\n\nSo N = 10201^4.\n\nNow factorize 10201. 10201 = 101^2? 101^2 = 10201. Yes!\n\nSo 10201 = 101^2, and 101 is prime.\n\nTherefore N = 101^8.\n\nThe sum of all prime factors (with multiplicity) = 101 × 8 = 808.\n\nLet me double-check: 101^2 = 10201. 10201^2 = 104060401. 104060401^2 = 10828567056280801.\n\nLet me verify 104060401^2:\n104060401 × 104060401.\n= 104060401 × 104000000 + 104060401 × 60401\n= 104060401 × 104000000 = 10822281704000000\n104060401 × 60401 = 104060401 × 60000 + 104060401 × 401\n= 6243624060000 + 41728220701\n= 6285352280701\n\nTotal = 10822281704000000 + 6285352280701 = 10828567056280801. ✓\n\nSo N = 101^8, and the sum of all prime factors (with multiplicity, \"not necessarily distinct\") = 8 × 101 = 808.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786629044}
